course: dictionary
lesson: 12546
title: Determination and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Determination is a noun. It names the firm choice to keep going, even when something is hard. «Maya had great determination and practised her spelling every night.» Practising every night when it is hard shows determination, so the word means not giving up.
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. In a story or on a sports field, determination means not giving up. In a science or formal question, «the determination of» means finding out or measuring something exactly. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Use the context to choose. Ask: is this about a person trying hard, or about finding something out exactly? If you swap in «not giving up» and the sentence still makes sense, you have the first meaning.
fact: Determination means being firm about doing something and not giving up, even when it is hard.
fact: «With determination» means trying hard and refusing to stop.
fact: «Sheer determination» means very great determination.
fact: In formal or science writing, «the determination of» means finding out or measuring something exactly.
fact: Determination is a noun, so you can describe it with words like «great» or «strong».
exercise: «Maya showed great determination in her training.» What does determination mean here? | A kind of food | *Being firm and not giving up | Measuring something exactly | Being sad about losing
exercise: «The determination of the winner took a long time.» What does determination mean here? | *Finding out exactly who won | Being firm about winning | Trying hard to win | Shouting loudly
exercise: «The scientist made a careful determination of the density.» What does determination mean here? | Giving up on the test | *Measuring something exactly | Telling a joke | Being stubborn about a hobby
test: Jo kept running with sheer determination, even when her legs ached. What does sheer determination show? | A map of the park | Feeling sleepy | *Very strong refusal to give up | Losing the race quickly
test: Sam practised piano with grit and determination. What does grit and determination mean? | Finding out a value exactly | Being quiet in class | Losing interest | *Firmness and not giving up
exam: Which meaning fits «shows great determination» in a school report? | An official decision about a winner | *Being firm and not giving up | Giving up on the task | Measuring something exactly
